  "evaluationNote": "CV F1 is the mean over 10 stratified group folds of the 362 training participants (also used for tuning). Test scores come from 90 held-out participants never used for training or tuning.",
  "limitations": [
    "Awakenings almost determines the label at the 85% cut-off (0 awakenings were always good sleepers, 2 or more always poor).",
    "Without awakenings, the lifestyle factors alone predict little better than guessing (F1 about 0.72 against a baseline of 0.71).",
    "One community sample of 452 people (ages 9 to 69); lifestyle inputs are self-reported 24-hour amounts, not timing.",
    "Predictions show statistical associations, not causes, and are not medical advice."
  ]
